error: an arena can only be reset where it is named

   ┌─ test/fail/12_reset_through_field.nul:11:5
   │
10 │ fn clear(b: *var Box) {
   │          ───────────  'b' is borrowed, so the arena inside it has no name here
11 │     b.arena.reset()
   │     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^  this releases an arena this function cannot name
   │
   = note: 'reset' proves that nothing in the arena is used afterward, and that
           proof compares names inside one function. Values in 'b.arena' live
           wherever the arena has been passed, and 'clear' can see almost none
           of them.
   = help: reset the arena where it was created, and leave 'clear' to do the work
           that does not release memory
